note: or_else error recovery pattern

set number a to 10
set number b to 0
set number result to a / b or_else do:
    print("Division by zero failed; falling back to the default value")
    change result to -1
end
print(f"result = {result}")

note: when find fails to match it simply returns empty, without an exception -- or_else
note: only reacts when an exception is thrown, so or_else does not run in that case.
set str config to find "[num]+" from "no digits here"
if config is empty do:
    change config to "default_mode"
end
print(f"config = {config}")

note: conversely, a real exception (an out-of-range index) does run or_else
set list items to ["a", "b", "c"]
set str safe_item to items[99] or_else do:
    change safe_item to "(none)"
end
print(f"safe_item = {safe_item}")
